Z||000003||Bluebottlejunky||08-23-2001||11:39 PM||||Yes, I replaced the gaskets, and for the valve covers I used the blue gaskets not the crapy..cork ones..Im pretty (almost very) sure that no vaccum lines in plastic lines..I have two soft codes witch means no light just stored. right now a 25/35 i think its IAC and MAT (replaced mat)...Would it be cause I didnt use a torque wrench on the parts? im pretty damn sure I put them on tight enuff?  Like the manifolds built up pressure then cant hold it and release?? thanks everyone.<BR>PS..no the car dosen't shake..it just dosent have power at like 3500 or when the shift light comes on it seems..<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B><p>[This message has been edited by Bluebottlejunky (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
