Z||000007||p4n1c||08-24-2001||10:07 AM||||I'd pull out the old torque wrench and check to see what you have torqued the bolts to.  It could very well be a loose bolt, especially if it's venting at high pressure.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||08-24-2001||11:05 AM||||Is the large tube that plugs into the back side of the TB seated tightly? This will cause a vacuum leak. How did the EGR tube look when you removed/re-installed it? When you had the intake apart did you disconnect the injector harness'. If you swapped left and right that will cause wierd bogging problems. I would also re-check the vacuum line connections. If you take a can of carb cleaner and lightly spray at the plenum/manifold joints, You can tell if you have a leak by the engine rpm. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||08-24-2001||12:47 PM||||Could be the TPS.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Bluebottlejunky||08-24-2001||05:05 PM||||Oreif, Yes that back tube is in tight from what I can see..and the EGR and EGR valve are new..so there not cracked..pretty sure all plastic lines are a-ok<BR>"When you had the intake apart did you disconnect the injector harness'. If you swapped left and right that will cause wierd bogging problems. "  no, what i did is take out injectors and fuel rail..and complete harness put it right away in a box...so i wouldnt ruin it.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> im kinda thinking tps sensor?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B>||||reg||1
